Dear Michael, dear Amanda,

RheinMain cannot accept a three-way split of the governing law. As a compromise, our client is prepared to use the law of England and Wales for the agreement and the related non-contractual obligations, subject to a final review of the parent-guarantee form. The corporate-authority opinion may of course address Delaware law without changing the law governing the guarantee itself.

We can accept an indemnity for proven product-defect and intellectual-property claims, provided that deployment errors, third-party software and unauthorised modifications remain outside RheinMain's responsibility. On consequential loss, we suggest a clause preserving liability that cannot lawfully be excluded and covering fraud, wilful concealment, death and personal injury.

We will send a clean comparison and redline by 12 April. Please reserve 22 April for the London signing meeting, subject to final board approval on both sides.

Yours sincerely,

